    "summary": "Built the pure \u00a73 ruins. New code: packages/content/src/ruins (the constants and the zod ruinRulesSchema/validateRuinRules, with a test) and packages/simulation/src/ruins (seeded sequence and navigation generation, clueFor, reportPresence/openRuin/answerRuin with sources-unlocked and gold-awarded events, and per-(player, ruin) lockouts). Tests: puzzles.test.ts covers generation, no-leak and timing over 500 seeds with evaluators written in the test file. operations.test.ts has the scripted solving and refusal cases for both kinds. determinism.test.ts covers hash coverage and a seeded session replay. Also added docs/ruins.md and one ./ruins subpath export each in packages/simulation/package.json and packages/content/package.json. After npm ci, I ran npm run typecheck, npm run test:unit (28 files, 560 tests), npm run test:integration (6 files, 36 tests) and npm run build (smoke passed). All exited 0. I also loaded both new subpaths from dist/ by hand with node. Measured: the best hint-ignoring sequence guesser averages about 178 s (10th percentile 30 s), and the shortest-first navigation guesser averages about 2222 s (10th percentile 303 s).",
